Task #4: Business API platform — sell API access to developers

## What was built
Full WhatsApp Business API-equivalent platform for VipChat:

### Backend
- 3 new DB models: ApiClient, ApiSubscription, ApiUsageLog (models.py)
- Idempotent SQL migrations for all 3 tables (__init__.py)
- /api/platform blueprint (api_platform.py):
  - POST /register — create API client, get key once
  - GET /me — client info + subscription
  - POST /rotate-key — invalidate old key, issue new one
  - PUT /webhook — configure HTTPS webhook URL
  - GET /usage — 14-day stats, daily chart data, recent logs
  - POST /subscribe — Stripe checkout session (demo fallback if no Stripe key)
  - POST /stripe-webhook — handle subscription lifecycle events
  - GET|PUT /admin/clients — admin list + suspend/reinstate
- /v1/ blueprint (business_api_v1.py) — 8 REST endpoints:
  - POST /v1/messages/send, GET /v1/messages
  - POST /v1/contacts/import, GET /v1/contacts
  - POST /v1/groups/create
  - POST /v1/broadcasts/send
  - GET /v1/analytics
  - POST /v1/webhooks/configure
  - GET /v1/account
- API key auth: vck_live_ prefix + 32 hex bytes, stored as SHA-256 hash
- Per-tier rate limiting: Starter 100/day, Pro 10k/day, Enterprise unlimited
- X-RateLimit-* headers on all message endpoints
- deliver_webhook() with HMAC-SHA256 signing + 3-retry background thread

### Frontend
- /api-platform route added to App.js (protected)
- ApiPlatformPage.js — full developer portal with 6 tabs:
  - Overview: hero CTA, stats cards, quick start curl example
  - API Docs: all 8 endpoints expandable with request/response + curl
  - API Keys: key display, rotate, client details, security warning
  - Usage: bar chart, daily table, recent API call log
  - Webhook: URL config, secret display, signature verification example
  - Billing: 3-tier pricing cards, upgrade flow, subscription info
- AdminPage.js: "API Clients" tab — table with tier, today's messages,
  total calls, status; suspend/reinstate controls; search; pagination
